{"id": "xjordan", "name": "Dana Biosphere Reserve", "short": "Dana Reserve", "place": "Jordan", "lat": 30.69, "lon": 35.57, "side": "r", "cont": "Asia", "country": "Jordan", "kind": "Desert", "park": true, "blurb": "Cliff-dwelling ibex, wolves and juniper where mountains drop to desert.", "tip": {"id": "rain", "title": "Fail the winter rains", "text": "The reserve drops from a high plateau to the low desert. Set Winter rainfall to -100% and watch the grasses and trees, then the ibex, birds and predators that rely on them."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Dana Biosphere Reserve", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dana_Biosphere_Reserve"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Nubian ibex", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nubian_ibex"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Rock hyrax", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_hyrax"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Tristram's starling", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tristram%27s_starling"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Arabian wolf", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arabian_wolf"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Caracal", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caracal"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Dana Biosphere Reserve", "icon": "quad", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "barley", "sp": "hordeum spontaneum", "xh": 0.12}, {"id": "juniper", "sp": "juniperus phoenicea", "xh": 0.37}, {"id": "pistacia", "sp": "pistacia atlantica", "xh": 0.62}, {"id": "acacia", "sp": "vachellia", "xh": 0.87}, {"id": "ibex", "sp": "capra nubiana", "xh": 0.06, "ic": "quad"}, {"id": "hyrax", "sp": "procavia capensis", "xh": 0.22, "desc": "Lives in colonies in rocky crevices and eats a wide range of plants. In the Middle East few land predators take it, helped by its sentries and refuges."}, {"id": "jird", "sp": "meriones tristrami", "xh": 0.38}, {"id": "chukar", "sp": "alectoris chukar", "xh": 0.54, "desc": "A rocky-slope game bird that eats a broad range of seeds and some insects. Golden eagles sometimes prey on it."}, {"id": "starling", "sp": "onychognathus tristramii", "xh": 0.7}, {"id": "blackbird", "sp": "turdus merula", "xh": 0.86}, {"id": "fox", "sp": "vulpes vulpes", "xh": 0.1, "wiki": "Red fox", "desc": "A small canid recorded in the area. GloBI lists it eating chukar, Tristram's jird and blackbirds."}, {"id": "jackal", "sp": "canis aureus", "xh": 0.3, "desc": "An opportunistic canid. GloBI lists it eating chukar, jirds and blackbirds, and it also scavenges carrion."}, {"id": "kestrel", "sp": "falco tinnunculus", "xh": 0.6}, {"id": "buzzard", "sp": "buteo buteo", "xh": 0.84, "desc": "A raptor recorded in the area. GloBI lists chukar and rodents such as the jird among its prey."}, {"id": "wolf", "sp": "canis lupus", "xh": 0.3, "name": "Arabian wolf", "wiki": "Arabian wolf", "desc": "The area's top predator. It takes ibex and smaller prey such as rodents and birds, and eats carrion. Wolves in Jordan are persecuted for killing livestock.", "no": ["badge"]}, {"id": "caracal", "sp": "caracal caracal", "xh": 0.7, "desc": "A cat Wikipedia lists as a threatened native of Dana. Small mammals make up most of its diet, and it can leap to catch birds.", "no": ["badge"]}, {"id": "sun", "sp": "sunlight", "xh": 0.1, "desc": "Strong sun and dry heat drive plant growth in the lower, desert parts of the reserve."}, {"id": "rain", "sp": "winter rainfall", "xh": 0.3, "desc": "Rain on the high plateau feeds the grasses and trees of the slopes. Dana drops from about 1,500 m to the low desert of Wadi Araba."}, {"id": "soil", "sp": "rocky soil", "xh": 0.5, "desc": "Thin soils on rock and sandstone slopes hold the reserve's 703 recorded plant species."}, {"id": "decomp", "sp": "decomposer community", "xh": 0.8, "name": "Soil microbes & insects", "desc": "Break down dead plants, dung and carcasses and 